1899–1900 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s twelfth season of competitive football. They competed in the [[Scottish First Division]], in which they ended runners-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1900.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1899-00|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> They won the Scottish Cup for the second season in a row, defeating Queen's Park 4–3. It was the seventh major domestic competition won by Celtic.

Forward [[Sandy McMahon]], who had been playing for the club since 1890, became the club's third ever captain, following [[Dan Doyle (footballer)|Dan Doyle]]'s retirement.

